# What Prettier does not own in this repository (MUSE-58).
#
# Every entry below is a file a formatter run would *damage*, not merely churn, and each
# one is asserted to still be ignored by `test/format.test.ts` — so an entry that stops
# mattering is a red test rather than a line nobody re-reads.
#
# `src/lib/sanity/sanity.types.ts` is deliberately **not** here. It is generated, and
# `sanity typegen` resolves `prettier.config.mjs` for it, which `.prettierignore` cannot
# reach; it is pinned by an `overrides` entry there instead and left checkable, because a
# full `prettier --check` on it is what proves the pin still matches the generator.

# Builds, caches and dependency trees.
dist/
.astro/
.sanity/
node_modules/

# Another checkout of this repository, agent-owned and transient.
.claude/worktrees/

# Generated artefacts. `sanity/schema.json` and `sanity/schema.stamp.json` are fingerprinted
# by `scripts/check-sanity.mjs`; reformatting either fails `npm run build` for no reason.
package-lock.json
sanity/schema.json
sanity/schema.stamp.json

# `.astro` has no parser installed. Prettier answers "No parser could be inferred" for all
# 22 of them, which makes `prettier --write .` *fail* rather than skip — so they are named
# here instead. The fix would be `prettier-plugin-astro`, which is not in the lockfile: it
# appears only as an optional peer of the Astro language tools and is not installed, so
# adding it is a new dependency, and the quote convention in the half that matters (the
# frontmatter) is already checked without it by `scripts/check-format.mjs`. If the plugin is
# ever added, `test/format.test.ts` fails and says to widen the rule to the markup half.
*.astro

# Prose. Where a paragraph wraps is a judgement, and `CLAUDE.md` is edited by every branch
# at once — a reflow of it conflicts with all of them. `npm run format:check` still holds
# these to tabs, line endings and trailing whitespace.
*.md

# `src/styles/tokens.css` is a hand-aligned column of brand values whose hex is uppercase to
# match the design system document it is transcribed from (`muse-design-system.md` §colour).
# Prettier collapses the alignment and lowercases all of it: 343 lines of one file, erasing
# the only thing that makes the table readable against its source. CSS formatting is not
# worth that, and the design system has its own gate in `npm run ds`.
*.css
